ualitative and quantitative technique.</article-title><source>Journal of Zoology</source><volume>231</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>248</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000672-Kunz1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kunz</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitaker</surname><given-names>JO</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>An evaluation of fecal analysis for determining food habits of insectivorous bats.</article-title><source>Canadian Journal of Zoology</source><volume>61</volume><fpage>1317</fpage><lpage>1321</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000672-MacArthur1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacArthur</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><year>1972</year><source>Geographical Ecology</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Harper and Row</publisher-name><fpage>269</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000672-IUCN2"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>IUCN</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>IUCN Red List of Threatened Species.</article-title><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="www.iucnredlist.org">www.iucnredlist.org</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000672-Hoofer1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoofer</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Van den Bussche</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Molecular phylogenetics of the chiropteran family Vespertilionidae.</article-title><source>Acta Chiropterologica</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>59</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000672-Ruedi1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-